cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "interactor-see-through-python: single-image layer decomposition, on the command bus"
abstract: >
  The reference half of the see-through A/B. One command in, reply bytes out,
  over the harness command bus, on the PyTorch pipeline and iceoryx2's Python
  binding -- sharing nothing with the C++ half but the wire between them, which
  is what lets the two disagree.
authors:
  - family-names: Lee
    given-names: "K. S. Ernest (iFire)"
    email: ernest.lee@chibifire.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4570-1436"
version: 0.1.0-dev.1
date-released: "2026-08-17"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/v-sekai-multiplayer-fabric/interactor-see-through-python"
keywords:
  - layer-decomposition
  - diffusion
  - anime
  - iceoryx2
  - runpod

# What this repository is built on: the design it serves, the contracts it vendors, and the
# transport layer whose image carries it.
references:

  - type: article
    title: "See-through: Single-image Layer Decomposition for Anime Characters"
    authors:
      - family-names: Lin
        given-names: Jian
      - family-names: Li
        given-names: Chengze
      - family-names: Qin
        given-names: Haoyun
      - family-names: Chan
        given-names: "Kwun Wang"
      - family-names: Jin
        given-names: Yanghua
      - family-names: Liu
        given-names: Hanyuan
      - family-names: Choy
        given-names: "Chun Wang Stephen"
      - family-names: Liu
        given-names: Xueting
    year: 2026
    doi: "10.1145/3799902.3811209"
    publisher:
      name: "Association for Computing Machinery"
    notes: >
      The design this interactor serves: one image of an anime character in,
      the layers it is composed of out, with depth ordering. The production
      settings this repository gates on are that pipeline's, not this one's.

  - type: software
    title: "contract-bus: the weft plane harness, the iceoryx2 C ABI as a dlsym dispatch table"
    authors:
      - family-names: Lee
        given-names: "K. S. Ernest (iFire)"
        orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4570-1436"
    year: 2026
    url: "https://github.com/v-sekai-multiplayer-fabric/contract-bus"
    notes: >
      Vendored as third_party/harness. weft/command.hpp decides the service
      names, the weft::byte payload and the request-id envelope; weft/limits.hpp
      decides the 128 KiB bound on one message.

  - type: software
    title: "transport-runpod: the RunPod Serverless transport layer"
    authors:
      - family-names: Lee
        given-names: "K. S. Ernest (iFire)"
        orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4570-1436"
    year: 2026
    url: "https://github.com/v-sekai-multiplayer-fabric/transport-runpod"
    notes: >
      What puts a RunPod job on the bus this interactor answers on. Its image is
      the base of this one's, so the job loop is taken rather than rebuilt.

  - type: software
    title: "interactor-see-through-cpp: the ggml half of the same A/B"
    authors:
      - family-names: Lee
        given-names: "K. S. Ernest (iFire)"
        orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4570-1436"
    year: 2026
    url: "https://github.com/v-sekai-multiplayer-fabric/interactor-see-through-cpp"
    notes: >
      The other implementation. proof/test_agreement.py reads its gate constants
      out of include/seethrough/command.h and fails when they differ from this
      one's.

  - type: software
    title: "iceoryx2: lock-free zero-copy inter-process communication"
    authors:
      - name: "Contributors to the Eclipse Foundation"
    year: 2026
    version: "0.9.3"
    license: Apache-2.0
    url: "https://github.com/eclipse-iceoryx/iceoryx2"
    notes: >
      The bus, through its PyPI binding, pinned to the version contract-bus
      transcribed its C ABI from. The binding names the payload type after the
      ctypes type, so weft_harness/bus.py sets it to weft::byte explicitly.
